WEBVTT

00:00:00.040 --> 00:00:03.080
Fifteen everyday habits can tell a burglar you

00:00:03.080 --> 00:00:06.230
live alone, and each has a simple fix,

00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:07.750
most of them free.

00:00:08.050 --> 00:00:10.790
Picture a stranger ambling past your home,

00:00:10.930 --> 00:00:12.150
eyes on a phone,

00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:15.030
in no hurry. He reads the mailbox,

00:00:15.080 --> 00:00:17.910
the doormat, the lone car in the drive.

00:00:18.190 --> 00:00:20.110
You never raised a blind or spoke to

00:00:20.110 --> 00:00:22.870
him, yet he now knows your routine.

00:00:23.030 --> 00:00:24.470
Your house told him.

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:26.390
Nobody likes that part.

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:29.040
A stranger needn't say hello to learn you're

00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:31.560
on your own, since your home keeps announcing

00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:33.980
it, in a language most of us never

00:00:33.980 --> 00:00:36.630
studied. I'm Diane Kowalski,

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:38.750
and I make videos about keeping a home

00:00:38.750 --> 00:00:40.390
safe when you live solo.

00:00:40.830 --> 00:00:42.790
I'm not a security professional,

00:00:42.850 --> 00:00:44.990
so for questions about your own doors and

00:00:44.990 --> 00:00:48.470
locks, ask a locksmith or your local police.

